"parse_workflow(text: str) -> workflow: WorkflowDocument":
  location: parse_workflow.py
  annotations: |
    Structurally parse a rendered workflow-file text into a
    `WorkflowDocument`. Accept the rendered text (rendering happens before
    parsing — the caller renders), parse it as YAML, validate the expected
    keys and field types, build `WorkflowStage` instances per entry, and
    return the aggregated `WorkflowDocument`. No content validation beyond
    the structural schema (key set, types, loop bounds); no agent-name
    resolution, no loop expansion, no depends_on rewriting — all of those are
    the compiler's responsibility.

    `text`: the rendered workflow-file text
    `workflow`: the parsed `WorkflowDocument` carrying declarative
                instructions for the compiler

    Algorithm:
    1. Accept the rendered `text`
    2. Parse the text as YAML. On invalid YAML — raise a structural
       error "invalid YAML in workflow-file"
    3. If the loaded value is not a dict (e.g. a scalar, a string, a list)
       — raise a structural error "workflow must be a mapping"
    4. Extract the optional top-level keys:
       - prompt: if present, must be a str; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-str value in workflow.prompt"
       - stages: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-mapping stages block in workflow"
       - extend: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-mapping extend block in workflow"
       - memory: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-mapping memory block in workflow"
       - profile: if present, must be a str; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-str value in workflow.profile". An empty or
         whitespace-only value normalizes to None
       - build: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-mapping build block in workflow"
       - assistants: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a
         structural error "non-mapping assistants block in workflow; author
         the map form keyed by assistant name"
       - delegation: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a
         structural error "non-mapping delegation block in workflow"
       - repeat: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-mapping repeat block in workflow"
       - gates: if present, must be a dict; otherwise raise a structural
         error "non-mapping gates block in workflow"
    5. For every other top-level key — raise a structural error
       "unknown key in workflow: KEY; valid keys: prompt, stages, extend,
       memory, profile, build, assistants, delegation, repeat, gates"
    6.0. For the memory block (when present), validate each key and value:
       - an unknown key raises "unknown key in workflow.memory: KEY; valid
         keys: method, path, max_rules, commit, mode"
       - method must be a str and one of "reflect"/"alignment"; otherwise
         raise "non-str value in workflow.memory.method" (non-str) or
         "method must be one of: reflect, alignment in workflow.memory"
         (str outside the set)
       - path must be a str of a valid path shape (non-empty, no leading "/",
         not absolute, no ".."); otherwise raise "non-str value in
         workflow.memory.path" (non-str) or "invalid path in
         workflow.memory.path: VALUE" (bad shape)
       - max_rules must be an int >= 1; otherwise raise "non-int value in
         workflow.memory.max_rules" (non-int) or "max_rules must be >= 1
         in workflow.memory" (int < 1)
       - commit must be a bool; otherwise raise "non-bool value in
         workflow.memory.commit"
       - mode must be a str and one of "r"/"w"/"rw"; otherwise raise
         "non-str value in workflow.memory.mode" (non-str) or "mode must
         be one of: r, w, rw in workflow.memory" (str outside the set).
         An authored mode together with the "reflect" method raises "mode
         is forbidden in workflow.memory with method: reflect"
       - build `WorkflowMemory` with materialized defaults (method "reflect",
         max_rules 25, commit False; mode "rw" under "alignment", None under
         "reflect")
    6.1. For each entry of stages (when present), identified by stage name
       and stage value:
       6.1.1. If the stage value is not a dict — raise a structural error
          "non-mapping stage NAME in workflow.stages"
       6.1.2. Validate the key set of the stage value against agent, env,
          prompt, loop, skills, skip, approve, manual, notes, reflect,
          memory, assistants, gates: an unknown key raises "unknown key in
          workflow.stages.NAME: KEY; valid keys: agent, env, prompt, loop,
          skills, skip, approve, manual, notes, reflect, memory,
          assistants, gates"
       6.1.3. agent (when present) must be a str; otherwise raise
          "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.agent"
       6.1.4. env (when present) must be a dict of str→str; a non-dict
          value raises a structural error "non-mapping env in
          workflow.stages.NAME"; a non-str key raises "non-str key in
          workflow.stages.NAME.env"; a non-str value raises "non-str
          value in workflow.stages.NAME.env.KEY". An empty map equals
          absence — build with env=None
       6.1.5. prompt (when present) must be a str; otherwise raise
          "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.prompt"
       6.1.6. loop (when present) must be an int and >= 1; otherwise raise
          "non-int value in workflow.stages.NAME.loop" (non-int) or
          "loop must be >= 1 in workflow.stages.NAME" (int < 1)
       6.1.7. skills (when present) must be a list[str]; otherwise raise
          "non-list-of-str skills in workflow.stages.NAME"
       6.1.8. skip (when present) must be a bool; otherwise raise a structural
          error "non-bool value in workflow.stages.NAME.skip"
       6.1.9. approve (when present) must be a str and one of "auto"/"plan"/"dialog";
          otherwise raise "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.approve"
          (non-str) or "approve must be one of: auto, plan, dialog in
          workflow.stages.NAME" (str outside the set)
       6.1.10. manual (when present) must be a bool; otherwise raise a structural
           error "non-bool value in workflow.stages.NAME.manual"
       6.1.11. notes (when present) must be a dict and every value must be a
           str; otherwise raise a structural error "non-mapping notes in
           workflow.stages.NAME" (non-dict) or "non-str value in
           workflow.stages.NAME.notes.KEY" (non-str value). An empty map equals
           absence — build with notes=None
       6.1.12. reflect (when present) must be a dict with a key set within
           {file, mode}: a non-dict value raises "non-mapping reflect in
           workflow.stages.NAME"; an unknown key raises "unknown key in
           workflow.stages.NAME.reflect: KEY; valid keys: file, mode". file
           is required, a str of a valid path shape — a missing file raises
           "file is required in workflow.stages.NAME.reflect", a non-str
           value raises "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.reflect.file",
           a bad shape raises "invalid path in
           workflow.stages.NAME.reflect.file: VALUE". mode (when present)
           is a str and one of "r"/"w"/"rw" — otherwise raise "non-str
           value in workflow.stages.NAME.reflect.mode" (non-str) or "mode
           must be one of: r, w, rw in workflow.stages.NAME.reflect" (str
           outside the set). Build `WorkflowReflect` with the authored
           file and mode materialized to "rw" when absent
       6.1.13. memory (when present) must be a bool; otherwise raise
           "non-bool value in workflow.stages.NAME.memory". An explicit false
           equals absence — build with memory=None
       6.1.14. gates (when present) must be a list — a non-list value raises
           "non-list gates in workflow.stages.NAME"; an empty list equals
           absence (None). Validate each step:
           - a non-mapping step raises "non-mapping gate step in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]"
           - the step key set is {name, script, agent, timeout, prompt,
             env}; an unknown key raises "unknown key in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]: KEY; valid keys: name, script,
             agent, timeout, prompt, env"
           - name is required: a missing name raises "gates step without
             name in workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]"; a non-str value raises
             "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i].name"
           - exactly one of script/agent is required: both or neither
             raises "gates step must carry exactly one of script/agent in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]"
           - agent must be a non-empty string; otherwise raise "agent must
             be a non-empty string in workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]". script
             must be a non-empty string or a non-empty list of non-empty
             strings — a scalar outside that raises "script must be a
             non-empty string in workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]"; a list that
             is empty or carries a non-str or empty element raises "script
             must be a non-empty list of non-empty strings in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]". A list payload joins with
             newlines into ONE multi-line script string (shell-identical to
             authoring the same text as a block scalar)
           - timeout/prompt (when present) must be a str; otherwise
             raise "non-str value in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i].timeout" / ".prompt"
           - prompt requires an agent step: a prompt authored on a step
             carrying script raises "prompt is forbidden on a script gate
             step in workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]" (the engine accepts
             prompt on AI steps only)
           - env (when present) must be a dict of str→str — valid on BOTH
             step kinds (the string-map pattern of the per-stage env): a
             non-dict value raises "non-mapping env in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i]"; a non-str key raises
             "non-str key in workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i].env"; a
             non-str value raises "non-str value in
             workflow.stages.NAME.gates[i].env.KEY". An empty map equals
             absence — build with env=None
           - build a `WorkflowGateStep` list in authored order and thread it
             into the `WorkflowStage` construction of 6.1.15
       6.1.15. Build a `WorkflowStage` from the validated values (agent, env,
           prompt, loop, skills, skip, approve, manual, notes, reflect,
           memory, assistants, gates — the list built by 6.1.14); an absent
           manual key yields None (NOT False);
           an empty notes map yields None; an empty env map yields None; an
           empty assistants map yields None
    6.2. For each entry of extend (when present), identified by stage name
        and entry value:
        6.2.1. If the entry value is not a dict — raise a structural error
           "non-mapping extend entry NAME in workflow.extend"
        6.2.2. If the entry value contains a depends_on key — raise a structural
           error "depends_on is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.3. If the entry value contains a skip key — raise a structural
            error "skip is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.4. If the entry value contains a manual key — raise a structural
            error "manual is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.5. If the entry value contains a notes key — raise a structural
            error "notes is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.6. If the entry value contains a reflect key — raise a structural
            error "reflect is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.7. If the entry value contains a memory key — raise a structural
            error "memory is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.8. If the entry value contains an env key — raise a structural
            error "env is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.9. before (when present) must be a list[str]; otherwise raise
           "non-list-of-str before in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.10. after (when present) must be a list[str]; otherwise raise
           "non-list-of-str after in workflow.extend.NAME"
        6.2.11. agent (when present) must be a str; otherwise raise
           "non-str value in workflow.extend.NAME.agent"
        6.2.12. loop (when present) must be an int and >= 1; otherwise raise
           "non-int value in workflow.extend.NAME.loop" (non-int) or
           "loop must be >= 1 in workflow.extend.NAME" (int < 1)
        6.2.13. approve (when present) must be a str and one of "auto"/"plan"/"dialog";
           otherwise raise "non-str value in workflow.extend.NAME.approve"
           (non-str) or "approve must be one of: auto, plan, dialog in
           workflow.extend.NAME" (str outside the set)
        6.2.14. If neither before nor after is present — raise a structural error
           "extend entry NAME requires at least one of before/after"
        6.2.15. Other keys of the entry value are NOT validated (open-ended:
           title, prompt, skills, roles, communication, trigger — a full
           stage-body field — and any other stage field) and pass through
           verbatim
        6.2.16. Build a `WorkflowExtendStage` from the validated before/after,
           agent/loop/approve, and the REMAINING entry value (excluding before,
           after, agent, loop, approve, and depends_on) as body — agent/loop/
           approve are extracted into the model, not carried in body, so they
           never reach the flow-file as stray stage fields
    6.3.  Validate the correspondence between the materialized method and the
        per-stage instructions (the method is "reflect" when no block is
        authored):
        - a reflect instruction under "alignment" raises "reflect is forbidden
          in workflow.stages.NAME with method: alignment"
        - a memory instruction under "reflect" raises "memory is forbidden in
          workflow.stages.NAME with method: reflect"
    6.4. For the build block (when present), validate each key and value:
        - the strict key set is agent, env, review (with agent, env,
          additional with agent, env); an unknown key anywhere in the block
          raises "unknown key in workflow.build.KEY…: KEY; valid keys: agent,
          env, review.agent, review.env, review.additional.agent,
          review.additional.env" — proxy and hosts are unknown keys and
          therefore structural errors (the host launcher must not read
          workflow files)
        - agent values (root, review, review.additional) must be a str;
          otherwise raise "non-str value in workflow.build.agent" /
          "non-str value in workflow.build.review.agent" / "non-str value in
          workflow.build.review.additional.agent"
        - env maps (root, review, review.additional) follow the string-map
          pattern: a non-mapping value raises "non-mapping env in
          workflow.build" / "non-mapping env in workflow.build.review" /
          "non-mapping env in workflow.build.review.additional"; a non-str
          key raises "non-str key in workflow.build.env" (and the review /
          review.additional counterparts); a non-str value raises
          "non-str value in workflow.build.env.KEY" (and the review /
          review.additional counterparts)
        - build a `WorkflowBuild` from the validated six-field set
    6.5. For the assistants catalog (when present): the block must be a
        mapping keyed by assistant name (otherwise "non-mapping assistants
        block in workflow; author the map form keyed by assistant name");
        each entry value must be a mapping (otherwise "non-mapping
        assistant entry in workflow.assistants.NAME"). Entry value key set:
        prompt, skills, agent, delegate, env — an unknown key (including
        name, gate, and when) raises "unknown key in
        workflow.assistants.NAME: KEY; valid keys: prompt, skills, agent,
        delegate, env". prompt and agent (when present) are str; skills
        (when present) is a list[str] (an authored empty list is carried
        as an explicit empty value — an override that clears); delegate
        (when present) is a bool (absent builds None — not False); env
        (when present) is a str→str map (an authored empty map is
        carried as an explicit empty value — NOT normalized to absence).
        An entry may carry none of prompt/skills — an override-style
        entry; the effective-content requirement is enforced at
        compilation. Every entry key must match [A-Za-z0-9._-] and must
        not be "assistant" ("assistant name is reserved"); a key repeated
        across the catalog and any inline declaration raises "duplicate
        assistant name: NAME". Build a `WorkflowAssistant` per entry
        with the key as name
    6.6. For the delegation block (when present): the block must be a dict
        (otherwise "non-mapping delegation block in workflow"); the key set
        is depth, max_tasks — an unknown key raises "unknown key in
        workflow.delegation: KEY; valid keys: depth, max_tasks". depth
        (when present) must be an int >= 0; max_tasks (when present) must
        be an int >= 1. Build a `WorkflowDelegation` with max_tasks
        materialized to 50 when not authored
    6.7. For each stage entry carrying an assistants key: the value must
        be a mapping keyed by assistant name (otherwise "non-mapping
        assistants in workflow.stages.NAME; author the map form keyed by
        assistant name"); an empty map equals absence (None). Each entry
        value must be a mapping (otherwise "non-mapping assistant
        attachment in workflow.stages.NAME.ASSISTANT"). Every entry states
        when — a missing when raises "when is required in
        workflow.stages.NAME.assistants.ASSISTANT"; when must be one of
        start/checkpoints/finish/message. gate (when present) must be a
        bool. A
        value whose keys are within {gate, when} is a reference; a value
        carrying any further key is a full inline declaration (the catalog
        field set plus gate and when) — it MAY carry no prompt and no
        skills (an override-style inline declaration); the
        effective-content requirement is enforced at compilation. The
        empty-preservation and delegate rules of 6.5 apply verbatim to
        the inline field values.
        The name rules of 6.5 apply to every entry key; the duplicate-name
        rule counts an inline declaration against the catalog and every
        other inline declaration. Build a `WorkflowAssistant` per entry
        with the key as name
    6.8. An assistants key in an extend-entry raises a structural error
        "assistants is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME" — attachments of
        a new stage are authored in the stages block by the new stage's
        name
    6.9. For the repeat block (when present): the block must be a dict
        (otherwise "non-mapping repeat block in workflow"); the key set is
        max_cycles, keep_runs — an unknown key raises "unknown key in
        workflow.repeat: KEY; valid keys: max_cycles, keep_runs". Each
        value (when present) must be an int and not negative — otherwise
        raise "non-int value in workflow.repeat.max_cycles" / "non-int
        value in workflow.repeat.keep_runs" (non-int, a boolean included)
        or "max_cycles must be >= 0 in workflow.repeat" / "keep_runs must
        be >= 0 in workflow.repeat" (negative). Build a `WorkflowRepeat`
        from the authored values only; an empty block equals absence —
        carry repeat=None
    6.10. For the gates settings block (when present), validate each key and
        value:
       - an unknown key raises "unknown key in workflow.gates: KEY; valid
         keys: patience, max_iterations, fresh_correction"
       - patience/max_iterations must be an int >= 0 and not a bool;
         otherwise raise "non-int value in workflow.gates.KEY" (non-int, a
         boolean included) or "KEY must be >= 0 in workflow.gates"
         (negative)
       - fresh_correction must be a bool; otherwise raise "non-bool value
         in workflow.gates.fresh_correction"
       - an empty block equals absence — carry gates=None; otherwise build a
         `WorkflowGates` from the authored keys only
    6.11. A gates key in an extend-entry raises a structural error "gates
        is forbidden in workflow.extend.NAME" — checks of a new stage are
        authored in the stages block by the new stage's name
    7. If prompt is None AND stages is empty (no entries) AND extend is
       empty (no entries) AND memory is None AND build is None AND
       assistants is empty AND delegation is None AND repeat is None AND
       gates is None
       — raise a structural error "empty workflow — provide at least
       prompt, one stage, one extend entry, the memory block, the build
       block, the assistants block, the delegation block, the repeat
       block, or the gates block" (profile never rescues a workflow from
       emptiness — activation is not content)
    8. Return `WorkflowDocument` from the parsed prompt, stages, extend,
       memory, profile, build, assistants, delegation, repeat, and gates
       (the built `WorkflowGates`, or None)

    Apply `convention` for code style, exception message formatting, and
    docstring style.

    Requirements:
    - Top-level unknown keys are a structural error — only prompt, stages,
      extend, memory, profile, build, assistants, delegation, repeat, and
      gates are accepted
    - extend-entry depends_on is a structural error; before/after (when
      present) must be list[str]; at least one of before/after is required
    - extend-entry names are NOT validated against any pipeline here —
      unknown before/after names pass through; the compiler raises a
      structural error on a name absent from the pipeline and the
      extend-stages
    - Per-stage unknown keys are a structural error — only agent, env,
      prompt, loop, skills, skip, approve, manual, notes, reflect, memory,
      assistants, gates are accepted
    - stages.<name>.env (when present) must be a dict of str→str; a non-dict
      value raises "non-mapping env in workflow.stages.NAME"; a non-str
      key raises "non-str key in workflow.stages.NAME.env"; a non-str
      value raises "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.env.KEY"; an
      empty map equals absence (env=None). env is valid ONLY in the stages
      block — env in an extend-entry is a structural error
    - profile (when present) must be a str; a non-str value raises
      "non-str value in workflow.profile"; an empty or whitespace-only
      value normalizes to None
    - The build block carries the strict six-field set — agent, env,
      review.agent, review.env, review.additional.agent,
      review.additional.env; any other key of the block (including proxy
      and hosts) is a structural error — the host launcher must not read
      workflow files; env maps follow the string-map pattern (str
      keys, str values)
    - skip (when present) must be a bool; a non-bool value is a structural
      error
    - skip is forbidden in an extend-entry — a structural error (skip is
      defined only for existing pipeline stages via the stages block)
    - skills (when present) must be a list[str]; a non-list-of-str value is
      a structural error
    - loop must be an int >= 1; zero, negative values, and non-int types
      are structural errors
    - approve (stages-block entry AND inline extend) must be a str and one of
      "auto"/"plan"/"dialog"; any other value or a non-str is a structural error
    - manual is accepted ONLY in the stages block; a non-bool manual is a
      structural error; manual in an extend-entry is a structural error
    - notes (stages-block only) must be a dict of str→str; a non-dict value
      raises "non-mapping notes in workflow.stages.NAME"; a non-str value
      raises "non-str value in workflow.stages.NAME.notes.KEY"; an empty notes
      map is treated as absence (notes=None); notes in an extend-entry is a
      structural error
    - trigger in the stages block is an unknown-key structural error; trigger
      in an extend-entry body passes through verbatim (validated at compile
      time, not here)
    - An extend-entry's inline agent (when present) must be a str, its
      inline loop (when present) must be an int >= 1, and its inline
      approve (when present) must be a str and one of "auto"/"plan"/"dialog" —
      same type/value rules as the stages block; non-conforming values are
      structural errors
    - Inline agent/loop/approve of an extend-entry are EXTRACTED into the
      model and excluded from the verbatim body (like before/after) — they
      do not pass through as stage fields
    - Stage-name keys are NOT validated against any pipeline IN THIS CELL
      — unknown stage names pass through; the compiler raises a structural
      error on names absent from both the pipeline and the extend-stages
      (strict validation; it does not silently apply or ignore with a
      warning). This cell stays declarative — it does NOT
      validate names itself
    - A single workflow-file can apply to several pipelines ONLY when
      every name it references exists in each target pipeline; a name
      absent from a target pipeline is a structural error (not a silent
      warning+skip) — split or prune such workflows
    - A workflow-file with none of a prompt, any stage entries, any extend
      entries, the memory block, the build block, the assistants block, the
      delegation block, the repeat block, or the gates block is rejected —
      at least one must be present
    - A workflow consisting of the build block alone is valid
    - The assistants catalog grammar: a name-keyed mapping; each entry value
      carries the key set prompt, skills, agent, delegate, env; delegate is
      a bool; env is a str→str map (an authored empty map is an explicit
      override); gate and when are attachment keys —
      authoring either in the catalog is an unknown-key structural error;
      name is the map key — an inner name key is an unknown key
    - The delegation block grammar: the key set depth, max_tasks; depth is
      an int >= 0; max_tasks is an int >= 1; max_tasks materializes to 50
      when the block omits it
    - The stage attachment grammar: a name-keyed mapping; an empty map
      equals absence (None); each entry value is a mapping whose keys within
      {gate, when} form a reference and whose any further key forms a full
      inline declaration (the catalog key set plus gate and when); when is
      required on every entry and is one of
      start/checkpoints/finish/message; gate is a bool
    - An assistant entry (catalog or full inline) without prompt and
      without skills parses successfully — override-style authoring; the
      requirement that the EFFECTIVE entry resolve content is the
      compiler's structural check, not a parse rule
    - For assistant fields, presence is preserved: skills [] and env {}
      are explicit empty overrides; delegate absent is None
    - The repeat block grammar: a mapping whose key set is max_cycles,
      keep_runs; each value is an int >= 0 (a boolean is not an integer); a
      scalar block value is a structural error; an empty block equals
      absence
    - A workflow consisting of the repeat block alone is valid
    - A workflow consisting of the gates block alone is valid
    - gates is forbidden in an extend-entry — a structural error
    - prompt is forbidden on a script gate step — a structural error (the
      engine accepts prompt on AI steps only)
    - A gate step's env (when present) is a dict of str→str valid on BOTH
      step kinds; an empty map equals absence (env=None); the env key shape
      (a legal environment variable name) is NOT validated here — the gate
      wrapper generation rejects an illegal key with a strict pre-run error
    - A malformed timeout value and the name text content are NOT
      validated — passed through verbatim (value grammar is engine-owned)
    - Assistant names match [A-Za-z0-9._-], are not "assistant", and are
      unique across the catalog and every inline declaration — a repeated
      declaration name raises "duplicate assistant name: NAME"
    - assistants is forbidden in an extend-entry — attachments of a new
      stage are authored in the stages block by the new stage's name
    - A workflow consisting of the assistants block alone or the delegation
      block alone is valid
    - Reference names are not resolved here — the compiler raises on a name
      matching no declaration of the effective document
    - agent value is NOT validated against a known agent set; absence of
      the wrapper file is surfaced by afm at invocation time
    - prompt contents (top-level and per-stage) are NOT validated — passed
      through verbatim to the consumer
    - The memory block and both instructions are validated structurally: key
      sets, types, value domains, path shapes, and the method ↔ instruction
      correspondence
    - Defaults are materialized in the model, not omitted
    - An explicit memory: false equals absence — the model carries None
    - A workflow consisting of the memory block alone is valid
    - reflect and memory are forbidden in an extend entry — participation of a
      new stage is authored in the stages block by its name

    Constraints:
    - Do not resolve agent to a wrapper path here — the compiler performs
      that composition
    - Do not perform loop expansion here — the compiler expands based on the
      loop count
    - Do not rewrite depends_on here — the compiler handles external
      references after expansion
    - Do not validate stage names against any pipeline schema — the compiler
      performs the match (raising a structural error on names absent from
      both the pipeline and the extend-stages)
    - Do not DELETE a stage or RECONNECT dependents when skip is True —
      skip is a declarative instruction; the compiler performs the removal
      and reconnection
    - Do not act on approve here — it is declarative; the compiler applies
      the interactive-suppress / auto_approve logic
    - Do not act on manual here — it is declarative; the compiler applies the
      force / cancel logic
    - Do not emit or act on the buttons here — notes is declarative; the
      compiler emits the per-stage buttons field
    - Do not let an inline extend approve reach the extend-stage body —
      it is extracted into the model (like agent/loop)
    - Do not read files or render here — the caller owns both; `text`
      arrives already rendered
    - Do not accept YAML text whose root is not a mapping — that is a
      structural error
    - Do not compose the memory root prefix here — the consumer composes the
      final path
    - Do not decide block emission or stage participation here — the consumer
      decides both
    - Do not validate reflect/memory keys inside stage bodies here — stage bodies
      are the consumer's input, checked at compilation
    - Do not resolve attachment references or derive profile ids here — the
      compiler resolves a reference against the assistant names of the
      effective document and the delivery materializes the profile

"WorkflowSyntaxError(message: str)":
  location: parse_workflow.py
  annotations: |
    Structural error of workflow-file parsing — raised, never returned. The
    single exception type every structural rejection in this cell surfaces:
    `parse_workflow` raises it for grammar violations (unknown top-level key,
    malformed stages/extend/memory, an invalid build block, the empty-workflow
    rule) and `load_workflow` lets it propagate from the parse step after
    rendering. A ValueError subclass, so consumers can catch either the
    concrete type or ValueError — exported through the facade for exactly
    that catch.

    `message`: the human-readable structural error text (no payload, no
               extra state)

    Requirements:
    - Inherits ValueError; constructed with `message` only

    Constraints:
    - Do not carry structured error data — the message is the whole contract

"ProfileSource()":
  location: profile_source.py
  annotations: |
    str-backed Enum declaring the origin of a resolved profile. Modeled
    via the standard library enum module; str-mixin so values serialize
    as plain strings (per `convention`).
  properties:
    "PROJECT = \"project\"": |
      Origin = project-level <cwd>/.goga/profiles/ (committed).
    "HOME = \"home\"": |
      Origin = home-level ~/.goga/profiles/ (personal, carried in the
      decoded home bundle).

"ResolvedProfile(name: str, data: dict[str, Any], source: ProfileSource)":
  location: resolved_profile.py
  annotations: |
    The active profile as a single value: its name, its whole content
    mapping, and where it was found.

    `name`: the resolved profile name
    `data`: the entire profile content — every top-level key becomes a
            template variable at rendering
    `source`: where the profile was found — `ProfileSource` value

    Requirements:
    - Immutable frozen dataclass (frozen=True, kw_only=True), per
      `convention`

    Constraints:
    - Do not resolve wrappers, render templates, or apply the content
      anywhere here — consumers own both
  properties:
    "name -> str": |
      The resolved profile name.
    "data -> dict[str, Any]": |
      The entire profile content; the rendering context source.
    "source -> ProfileSource": |
      Origin of the profile: project or home.

"LoadedWorkflow(document: WorkflowDocument, profile: ResolvedProfile | None)":
  location: loaded_workflow.py
  annotations: |
    The result of loading a workflow-file under an activation context:
    the parsed document plus the profile that was active during the load
    (None when no profile resolved).

    `document`: the parsed `WorkflowDocument`
    `profile`: the `ResolvedProfile` active at rendering, or None

    Requirements:
    - Immutable frozen dataclass (frozen=True, kw_only=True), per
      `convention`

    Constraints:
    - Do not revalidate fields here — the parts were validated by their
      producers
  properties:
    "document -> WorkflowDocument": |
      The parsed workflow document.
    "profile -> ResolvedProfile | None": |
      The profile active during rendering, or None when the render ran
      with an empty context.

"WorkflowBuild(agent: str | None = None, env: dict[str, str] | None = None, review_agent: str | None = None, review_env: dict[str, str] | None = None, review_additional_agent: str | None = None, review_additional_env: dict[str, str] | None = None)":
  location: workflow_build.py
  annotations: |
    Data model of the top-level workflow build block — the strict
    six-field set of build-pass settings the workflow may provide. All
    fields default to None (absent); an absent field never overrides the
    configuration.

    `agent`: tasks-pass agent override, or None
    `env`: tasks-pass env overlay (string map), or None
    `review_agent`: review-pass agent override, or None
    `review_env`: review-pass env overlay, or None
    `review_additional_agent`: external-review agent override, or None
    `review_additional_env`: external-review env overlay, or None

    Requirements:
    - Use @dataclass(kw_only=True) (per `convention`)
    - Field order is fixed: agent, env, review_agent, review_env,
      review_additional_agent, review_additional_env
    - Built only by `parse_workflow` from the validated block

    Constraints:
    - Do not merge with any configuration here — the build path owns the
      layering
    - No proxy, hosts, or any other field may appear — the parser
      rejects unknown keys of the block as structural errors
  properties:
    "agent -> str | None": |
      Tasks-pass agent override; None when absent.
    "env -> dict[str, str] | None": |
      Tasks-pass env overlay; None when absent.
    "review_agent -> str | None": |
      Review-pass agent override; None when absent.
    "review_env -> dict[str, str] | None": |
      Review-pass env overlay; None when absent.
    "review_additional_agent -> str | None": |
      External-review agent override; None when absent.
    "review_additional_env -> dict[str, str] | None": |
      External-review env overlay; None when absent.

"load_home_profiles(home_dir: Path) -> profiles: dict[str, dict[str, Any]]":
  location: load_home_profiles.py
  annotations: |
    Read and strictly parse the whole home profiles bundle: every flat
    *.yml file under `home_dir`, collected into one name → mapping.

    `home_dir`: the home profiles directory (typically
                ~/.goga/profiles/)
    `profiles`: mapping of profile name → profile content

    Algorithm:
    1. Scan flat *.yml files (non-recursive) under `home_dir`; a missing
       directory resolves to an empty mapping
    2. For each file: parse as YAML; invalid YAML, a non-mapping root,
       or a non-string key raises one strict error naming the file path
       (the JSON carriage would silently coerce a non-string key,
       mutating the profile across the docker boundary)
    3. For each parsed mapping: reject a value no JSON payload can
       represent (e.g. an unquoted YAML date) with one strict error
       naming the file path — the bundle crosses the docker boundary as
       JSON, so this is part of malformed-profile strictness, not
       content validation
    4. Return the collected mapping (file stem → content)

    Requirements:
    - A malformed home profile is a strict failure — the caller runs this
       on the host before any container launches
    - Deterministic — unchanged directory contents produce the identical
       mapping

    Constraints:
    - Do not read the environment — the directory arrives as a parameter
    - Do not validate profile-name grammar here — bundle keys that fail
      the grammar are inert; the lookup validates the REQUESTED name

"resolve_profile(name: str, project_dir: Path, home_profiles: dict[str, dict[str, Any]]) -> profile: ResolvedProfile":
  location: resolve_profile.py
  annotations: |
    Validate a profile name and resolve it to a `ResolvedProfile`:
    project lookup first, then the home bundle; on the same name the
    project profile wins.

    `name`: the requested profile name
    `project_dir`: the project profiles directory (typically
                   <cwd>/.goga/profiles/)
    `home_profiles`: the decoded home bundle mapping
    `profile`: the resolved `ResolvedProfile`

    Algorithm:
    1. Validate `name` against the profile-name grammar
       ([A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*; "." and ".." forbidden) — the name
       becomes a filesystem path component, so a violation raises one
       strict error naming the profile (path-traversal guard)
    2. When <project_dir>/<name>.yml exists: parse it; invalid YAML, a
       non-mapping root, or a non-string key raises one strict error
       naming the profile and the path (the rendering context is keyword
       arguments — a non-string key would crash the render); return
       `ResolvedProfile` with source project
    3. Otherwise, when `name` is present in `home_profiles`: return
       `ResolvedProfile` with source home
    4. Otherwise raise one strict error naming the profile and BOTH
       lookup locations

    Requirements:
    - Project-wins on the same name
    - All failures are strict, pre-run, with actionable messages

    Constraints:
    - Do not read the environment — home data arrives as a parameter
    - Do not render anything here — the consumer renders

"render_workflow(text: str, profile_data: dict[str, Any], source_name: str = \"\") -> rendered: str":
  location: render_workflow.py
  annotations: |
    Render a whole workflow-file text as a Jinja template with the
    active profile content as the template context. Rendering is a step
    BEFORE parsing; the rendered text feeds the standard parser.

    `text`: the raw workflow-file text
    `profile_data`: the template context — the entire active profile
                    content, or an empty mapping for a context-less
                    render
    `source_name`: optional workflow file name carried into error
                   messages
    `rendered`: the rendered text

    Use `jinja2` for the environment configuration and the error
    surfacing.

    Algorithm:
    1. Build the rendering environment per `jinja2` — the fixed flag
       set, the standard Undefined, autoescape off
    2. Render the whole text with `profile_data` as the context
    3. A template syntax error raises one strict error carrying
       `source_name`, the line number, and the message

    Requirements:
    - A plain file without template syntax renders to itself
    - Missing context keys follow standard Jinja semantics — falsy in
      guards, empty when interpolated; nested access on a missing key
      fails at render time

    Constraints:
    - Do not parse YAML here — the consumer parses the rendered text
    - Do not read files or the environment — text and context arrive as
      parameters

"resolve_activation(cli_profile: str | None, env_profile: str | None, workflow_default: str | None) -> name: str | None":
  location: resolve_activation.py
  annotations: |
    Resolve the effective profile name from the three activation
    sources, strongest first: CLI option, environment variable,
    workflow default.

    `cli_profile`: the --profile flag value, or None
    `env_profile`: the GOGA_PROFILE value, or None
    `workflow_default`: the workflow's top-level profile: default, or
                        None
    `name`: the effective profile name, or None when every source is
            unset

    Algorithm:
    1. Return the first non-empty value among `cli_profile`,
       `env_profile`, `workflow_default` — in that order
    2. Empty and whitespace-only strings count as unset
    3. Return None when all sources are unset

    Requirements:
    - Pure — no environment reads; every source arrives as a parameter

    Constraints:
    - Do not load the profile here — only the name resolves

"load_workflow(workflow_path: Path, cli_profile: str | None = None, env_profile: str | None = None, home_profiles: dict[str, dict[str, Any]] | None = None) -> loaded: LoadedWorkflow":
  location: load_workflow.py
  annotations: |
    The single loading chain that turns a workflow-file path into a
    `LoadedWorkflow` under an activation context: read, peek the
    default, resolve activation, resolve the profile, render the whole
    file, parse the rendered text.

    `workflow_path`: absolute path to the workflow-file
    `cli_profile`: the CLI activation channel value, or None
    `env_profile`: the environment activation channel value, or None
    `home_profiles`: the decoded home bundle, or None (treated as empty)
    `loaded`: the `LoadedWorkflow` — document plus the active profile

    Use `jinja2` (through `render_workflow`) for the rendering step.

    Algorithm:
    1. Read the file text; OSError propagates unchanged
    2. Peek a literal top-level profile: value from the RAW text — a
       default that materializes only through template rendering does
       not participate in activation
    3. Resolve the effective profile name via `resolve_activation` from
       the two channel values and the peeked default
    4. When a name resolved: load it via `resolve_profile` against
       <cwd>/.goga/profiles/ and the home bundle; otherwise the profile
       is None
    5. Render the whole text via `render_workflow` with the profile
       content as the context — an empty context when no profile
       resolved
    6. Parse the rendered text via `parse_workflow`; structural errors
       propagate with their readable messages
    7. Return `LoadedWorkflow` of the document and the profile

    Requirements:
    - Rendering runs ALWAYS — a plain file renders to itself; templates
      without activation render with the empty context
    - Rendering never bypasses validation — the rendered text passes
      the standard structural validation unchanged
    - The activation channels arrive as parameters — the chain reads no
      environment

    Constraints:
    - Do not mutate the inputs; do not write anything
    - Do not resolve the workflow path or its existence here — the
      caller owns path composition and guards

